{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling for the capture head 102169dd (checker question dfad64c7,\nreview request 05ff3c74), on the BR-4 partial under 15b0f8ab.\n\n1. Deadlines: accepted, both. The kill timer for each concurrent\n   replay child in local-archive-command.ts:78 goes from 30,000 to\n   90,000 ms, and the enclosing Grow production follower case in\n   archive-installed.test.ts:1607 from 30,000 to 100,000 ms. Both are\n   at least three times the median of the two complete follower\n   observations (25,668 and 29,457 ms; median 27,562.5; three times\n   82,687.5), the child timer was the cause of the failure at a5a29091,\n   and the outer case needs room for reporting and joined cleanup. The\n   Native producer, the clone and every production clock stay at\n   30,000 ms. b8a6c843 named the follower's deadline as one change\n   because the builder's question described one; the two edits are\n   the one repair. The PD-2 note records the sample, the median, the\n   factor and both values, each labelled by how it was taken.\n\n2. Testing rule: adopted in this head, scoped as written. The\n   paragraph in docs/testing.md (lines 338-344) states the offline\n   archive command's limit as at least three times its median, with\n   the enclosing follower's median bounding each child when only the\n   follower has timings, and reporting and cleanup inside the outer\n   allowance. That is the BR-4 condition made a rule for this command,\n   not a general change to the gate; keep it under the command's\n   heading, and keep the reason in the test comments too. docs/testing.md\n   was published by another actor, so the head's artifact filing must\n   name the docs directory; if it does not, the builder adds that\n   artifact before the verdict.\n\nEverything else in b8a6c843 stands: fresh ordinary gate at the exact\nhead, BR-4's other outcomes open under 15b0f8ab, and the capture\ncontrols (exact target identity, privacy, completeness, debit\npreservation) assessed at this head. The planner deploys dap-grow after\nlanding and reads the rows.","body":{"to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}